Heads of Department and Discipline Leads
(4)
Heads of Department and Discipline Leads are responsible for:
Providing oversight to ensure laboratory work is planned, risk assessed and is safely conducted;
Confirming the acceptance of residual risk for heightened risk activity;
Seeking assurance that there are adequate levels of supervision;
Seeking assurance that required inductions are completed for each discipline; and
Confirming that periodic laboratory inspections for hazard management and continuous improvement are completed.

Academic Staff (Course and Subject Coordinators)
(5)
Academic staff such as Course and Subject Coordinators are responsible for:
Ensuring laboratory work is planned, risk assessed and is safely conducted;
Accepting or querying the residual risk for heightened risk activity;
Ensuring adequate levels of supervision for all laboratory activities;
Ensuring that students have completed all required inductions before laboratory activity commences;
Leading or participating in periodic laboratory inspections for hazard management and continuous improvement.

Teaching Educators
(6)
Teaching Educators are responsible for:
Safely conducting laboratory work;
Ensuring operational risk controls are in place and working;
Ensuring students have completed the required inductions before commencing laboratory work;
Ensuring personal protective equipment (PPE) and general clothing requirements are strictly followed; and
Reporting all hazards and incidents.

Students
(8)
Students are responsible for:
Completing the mandatory safety induction before commencing laboratory activities;
Following the personal protective equipment (PPE) and general clothing requirements;
Following safe laboratory practices and processes;
Stopping the activity if there is immediate danger to health and safety; and
Reporting all hazards and incidents to teaching staff.

Health and Safety Team
(9)
The Health and Safety Team are responsible for:
Providing oversight and monitor this Procedure;
Advising on hazards and risk assessments as required;
Advising on risk control measures;
Supporting incident response, investigation, and sharing the lessons learnt across the organisation; and
Supporting periodic laboratory inspections for hazard management and continuous improvement.
